olset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback to v5.0.0 succeeded and is verified in all three regions. The incident was denied by a reviewer, who said it should be about `payments-worker`. I'll check that service before filing anything.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SBoxvJrsP1hkJotkrgKMZg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "`payments-worker` is also unhealthy, with the same 18% error rate, on v3.4.0. I'll check its release history to see whether it was also affected by this morning's deploy.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UwD2EMmTHPsiH8x2veJpDG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.8}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01UofPUrJnYxWgPhU7VLHDEv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker unhealthy on v3.4.0 (18% error rate)", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker is unhealthy in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) on v3.4.0, with an 18% error rate. v3.4.0 is marked unhealthy in production; the last healthy release is v3.3.0. Related: payments-api was rolled back from v5.1.0 to v5.0.0 for a similar error rate. Rollback of payments-worker has not been performed yet.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2", "confidence": 0.75}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled back `payments-api` to v5.0.0, and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 on `payments-worker`, which the reviewer directed.\n\n- **Rollback:** `payments-api` was on v5.1.0, which was degraded with an 18% error rate. It is now on v5.0.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, and the rollout is verified. v5.0.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Incident:** My first incident, for `payments-api`, was denied by a reviewer who said it should be about `payments-worker`. The reviewer approved INC-0001 for `payments-worker`. The on-call engineer was paged.\n- **Still unresolved:** `payments-worker` is unhealthy on v3.4.0 with the same 18% error rate. Its last healthy release is v3.3.0. I did not roll it back because you asked only about the payments service and the reviewer didn't ask for it. Tell me if you want v3.3.0 deployed there.\n\nThe service name \"payments\" wasn't recognized, so I matched it to `payments-api` and `payments-worker`. If you meant a different service, let me know.", "type": "text"}]}]}